The code statements that fix the bug are:
atomic_add(posted, &sc->recv_io.credits.available);
available = atomic_xchg(&sc->recv_io.credits.available, 0);
atomic_add(new_credits, &sc->recv_io.credits.count);  // inside manage_credits_prior_sending
Reason:
The fix introduces a dedicated atomic counter `credits.available` that is incremented only after recv buffers are successfully posted (in `smbd_post_send_credits`). In `manage_credits_prior_sending`, the availability is drained atomically via `atomic_xchg`, ensuring only truly available credits are granted. The `credits.count` is then incremented within the same function, and the separate `atomic_add` in `smbd_post_send_iter` is removed, eliminating the race condition.

